WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.050
(groovy music)

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:02.883
- All right y'all.

00:00:02.883 --> 00:00:03.795
Boop!

00:00:03.795 --> 00:00:04.720
(laughing)

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.880
I want to share one
last tidbit of goodness

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.220
before we wrap up this hour.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.027
This is "What I'm Liking" Lester.

00:00:10.027 --> 00:00:13.700
(groovy music)
(crowd cheering)

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.300
Listen, the pandemic has been hard

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.740
and few have had it harder than nurses.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.300
That's what makes this
story such a bright spot.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.100
When Kelsey, an ER nurse in Georgia,

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.610
got called up to the
hospital's rooftop helipad

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.450
she had no idea what would be in store.

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.290
She obviously assumed it would
be a pickup for a patient,

00:00:29.290 --> 00:00:31.100
a logical guess or assumption,

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.830
but nope, it was something else entirely.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.970
And the hospital staff,
actually they captured this.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.180
So watch this.

00:00:39.423 --> 00:00:42.173
(staff cheering)

00:00:43.163 --> 00:00:45.626
- [Woman] Oh my God!

00:00:45.626 --> 00:00:46.819
(staff crying)

00:00:46.819 --> 00:00:48.569
Oh, they are so nice.

00:00:49.768 --> 00:00:52.518
(staff cheering)

00:00:53.776 --> 00:00:54.609
(crowd cheering)

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:56.900
- Kelsey's boyfriend, Jacob, proposed

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.810
and she said yes.

00:00:58.810 --> 00:01:01.820
That would've been awkward if she hadn't.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.723
We have them on the line right now.

00:01:04.598 --> 00:01:05.931
What's up y'all?

00:01:07.131 --> 00:01:08.590
How are you doing Kelsey and Jacob?

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:11.810
So you're both nurses
and you met on the job.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.957
So thank you, first of
all, for being nurses.

00:01:13.957 --> 00:01:14.790
(crowd cheering)

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.748
Thank you so much.
- Of course.

00:01:16.748 --> 00:01:18.903
- And y'all met on the job, right?

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.840
- Yes, so I was a new grad
coming out of nursing school

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:25.120
and trying to decide
where I was gonna work at

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.060
and I interviewed at
Kennestone and they said

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.360
why don't you come shadow
on trauma for a night

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:30.450
and just see how you like it.

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.140
And they were smart putting
me with Jake for a night.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.230
And on our very first evening together

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:36.770
we got to go up to the helipad

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.470
and that's why it was really special

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.870
for years later, after
everything we've been through

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:44.010
and how much we've
grown and fallen in love

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:44.843
and everything else.

00:01:44.843 --> 00:01:46.630
For him to propose on the same helipad,

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:49.690
it was just a really sweet
full-circle moment for us.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.340
- Yes, I mean working with
my best friend is amazing,

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.730
especially in such a tough
time like the pandemic.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:56.780
It's very stressful.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:57.960
But being able to go to work

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.200
and come home with my best friend

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.188
and kind of wind down is amazing.

00:02:01.188 --> 00:02:02.280
(crowd cheering)
- Aww.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:03.540
I love y'all.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:04.660
I love love.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:06.710
So what were you thinking Kelsey

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.653
when you realized he was proposing?

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.830
- Um, honestly it took me
a second to even figure out

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:13.970
that's what he was doing.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.700
I was in shock completely.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.600
His biggest goal was to make me surprised

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.120
and boy did he achieve it.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.810
And he had it arranged

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.510
where our managers had us
off for the rest of the day

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.340
so we could go celebrate
with our friends and family.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.173
- [Kelly] Oh man.

00:02:26.173 --> 00:02:27.850
Well Jacob,
(crowd clapping)

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:29.440
you are a straight up baller.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:32.390
Arriving helicopter, proposing.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:33.920
I'm like wait what?

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.910
Like men everywhere right now are like

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:38.290
are you fricking serious?

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.980
I got to arrive on a helicopter.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:40.813
That's amazing.

00:02:40.813 --> 00:02:44.010
Were you nervous at all
or were you just excited?

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.330
- Kelly, you couldn't imagine

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.080
how much stress went into this bad boy.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.270
I mean, head to toe full body sweats.

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.470
Um...
(Kelly laughing)

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:53.530
So I had to make a fake patient
out of pillows and blankets.

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:55.400
I had to get the manager
team and the nurses

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.420
to all pretend that we're
in separate sections

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.080
and all that good stuff.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:00.470
And the whole time, the helicopter,

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.510
it's an active helicopter.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:04.100
So like if a 9-1-1 emergency gets called

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.400
whole plan's over with.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:06.660
We go somewhere else, you know?

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.780
So,

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:08.613
stressful,

00:03:08.613 --> 00:03:09.840
most stressful day of my entire life.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.960
But when I finally asked and she said yes

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.680
it was the best day of my life for sure.

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:15.130
- [Kelly] That's totally worth it.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.960
You two are adorable!
(crowd clapping)

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.880
Thank you so much Kelsey and Jake.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.230
And again, congratulations.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:22.440
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:23.273
- [Kelsey] Of course!

00:03:23.273 --> 00:03:24.293
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you so much!

00:03:24.293 --> 00:03:25.126
This is crazy.
(bell dinging)

00:03:25.126 --> 00:03:26.350
- [Kelly] Well that's not all.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:28.990
Our season long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:30.870
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.760
want to honor ultimate overachievers

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:36.130
and you're arriving in a
helicopter man, so that's you.

00:03:36.130 --> 00:03:38.020
So they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:38.926
How does that sound?

00:03:38.926 --> 00:03:39.880
(crowd cheering)

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:40.713
- That's awesome!

00:03:40.713 --> 00:03:41.580
Thank you so much.

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:42.525
That's amazing.
- Thank you!

00:03:42.525 --> 00:03:43.454
That's amazing.

00:03:43.454 --> 00:03:44.445
- Thank you.
- Weddings are expensive.

00:03:44.445 --> 00:03:45.310
Thank you (laughing).
- Thank you guys!

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:49.353
Congrats and good luck!
(crowd cheering)

